# Put the interfaces in their zones (this changes traffic at once):
#   zone FWS_Internal: no interface is known
#   zone FWS_External: no interface is known
# Written inactive:
#   Rule @900.0: not converted: source '$$ Management Servers': an alias, whose value is set per engine, and the input holds no engine; not converted: destination '$$ Local Cluster': an alias, whose value is set per engine, and the input holds no engine; references '$$ Management Servers': an alias, who
#   updates by name: 'updates.example.com (names)' holds members only its platform knows
#   vpn only: not converted: it matches traffic of VPNs only (Source VPN)
#   no social: no port mapping for application(s) Facebook; supply one with --app-map
#   helpdesk to dmz: source user match helpdesk is not converted
#   office web: schedule 'Office hours' is not converted; the rule would apply at all times
#   block list: not converted: it has a block list (it discards what the dynamic block list holds, and lets the rest go on)
#   lan but admins: service syslog-from-514: source ports, an ICMP code, SCTP ports or protocol 0, which a service object cannot say
